If necessary, clean off the balance pan with a soft painters brush.
如有必要，用软的漆刷把秤盘清扫干净。

31
00:02:22,010 --> 00:02:26,130
Make sure the doors are closed and press the control bar to tear the balance.
确保天平门已关好，然后按下控制键给天平去皮。

32
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:33,170
A reading of 0.0 milligrams with no other display should appear if the balance is stable.
如果天平稳定，应显示 0.0 毫克，并且没有其他显示。

33
00:02:33,170 --> 00:02:38,210
Simply place the object to be weighed in the center of the balance pan, close the doors,
只需把待称物体放在秤盘中央，关好天平门，

34
00:02:38,210 --> 00:02:42,770
and record the weight that is indicated on the display after the numbers have ceased
等显示屏上的数字不再

35
00:02:42,770 --> 00:02:44,250
to fluctuate.
波动后，记录显示的重量。

36
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:48,890
Remove the object from the balance pan and repeat the process two more times to ensure
把物体从秤盘上取下，再重复这个过程两次，以确保

37
00:02:48,890 --> 00:02:49,890
precision.
精密度。

38
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:54,370
Finally, average the three readings to determine the weight of the object.
最后，取三次读数的平均值，确定物体的重量。

39
00:02:54,370 --> 00:02:59,050
When weighing a chemical, care must be taken to never allow the chemical to touch the balance
称量化学品时，必须注意绝不能让化学品接触到

40
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:00,050
pan.
秤盘。

41
00:03:00,050 --> 00:03:03,650
Instead, weigh the chemical in an appropriate container.
而应当把化学品放在合适的容器里称量。

42
00:03:03,650 --> 00:03:08,330
If possible, weigh the chemical directly into the destination vessel.
如有可能，直接把化学品称入目标容器中。

43
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:12,530
This action eliminates a transfer step and the potential loss of material.
这样可以省去一个转移步骤，避免可能的物料损失。

44
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:17,810
If using the destination vessel is not possible, choose the smallest weigh boat or piece
如果无法使用目标容器，就选择能有效盛放所需量化学品的

45
00:03:17,810 --> 00:03:22,250
of weigh paper that will effectively hold the desired amount of chemical.
最小的称量舟或称量纸。

46
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:26,570
The heavier the container, the less accurate the measurement, because just a small weight
容器越重，测量就越不准确，因为这是在两个相对较大的数之间

47
00:03:26,570 --> 00:03:30,170
difference will exist between relatively large numbers.
求一个很小的重量差。

48
00:03:30,170 --> 00:03:35,130
In addition, the more surface area, the more places for chemicals to stick to instead of
此外，表面积越大，化学品就有越多的地方会粘附，而不是

49
00:03:35,130 --> 00:03:37,990
being transferred to the destination vessel.
被转移到目标容器中。

50
00:03:37,990 --> 00:03:43,290
Place the weighing container on the balance pan, close the doors, and tear the balance.
把称量容器放在秤盘上，关好天平门，然后去皮。

51
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:48,250
If you are using weigh paper, first crease the paper along the diagonal to facilitate
如果用称量纸，先沿对角线把纸折出折痕，以便

52
00:03:48,250 --> 00:03:50,530
the transfer of chemicals.
转移化学品。

53
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:54,530
Remove the weighing vessel from the balance and load an estimated amount of chemical
把称量容器从天平上取下，用刮刀往上面加

54
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:57,170
onto it with a spatula.
估计量的化学品。

55
00:03:57,170 --> 00:04:01,370
Place the loaded weighing vessel back on the balance pan and close the doors to obtain
把装好化学品的称量容器放回秤盘，关好天平门，

56
00:04:01,370 --> 00:04:02,370
a reading.
读取读数。

57
00:04:02,370 --> 00:04:07,130
If the weight is too high, take the weigh vessel off the balance pan and transfer the
如果重量太大，就把称量容器从秤盘上取下，把

58
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:12,330
excess chemical into an appropriate waste container, never back into the original reagent
多余的化学品转移到合适的废物容器中，绝不要倒回原来的试剂

59
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:13,330
bottle.
瓶。

60
00:04:13,330 --> 00:04:18,170
If the weight is too low, introduce more chemical to the weigh container.
如果重量太小，就往称量容器中再加一些化学品。

61
00:04:18,170 --> 00:04:23,170
Remove the weigh vessel from the balance pan every time additional chemical is introduced.
每次添加化学品时，都要把称量容器从秤盘上取下。

62
00:04:23,170 --> 00:04:28,350
Finally, transfer the chemical from the weigh paper or weigh boat into the appropriate reaction
最后，把化学品从称量纸或称量舟转移到合适的反应

63
00:04:28,350 --> 00:04:29,350
vessel.
容器中。

64
00:04:29,350 --> 00:04:34,090
Re-weigh the paper or boat to determine the exact amount of chemical that was transferred.
再次称量称量纸或称量舟，以确定实际转移的化学品的准确量。

65
00:04:34,090 --> 00:04:39,130
After finishing with the balance, use a soft brush to clean up any solids from the balance
用完天平后，用软刷清扫秤盘上的固体，

66
00:04:39,130 --> 00:04:41,410
pan and wipe up any liquids.
并擦去任何液体。

67
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:45,490
Close the doors to prevent dust and dirt from entering the balance.
关好天平门，防止灰尘和污物进入天平。

68
00:04:45,490 --> 00:04:49,770
Clean the surrounding area and remove all items that you brought there.
清理周围区域，拿走你带来的所有物品。

69
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:54,370
Keep the balance and area surrounding it in better shape than when you found it.
让天平及其周围区域保持得比你来时更好。

70
00:04:54,370 --> 00:04:59,690
The accuracy of your measurements depends on both good technique and environmental factors.
测量的准确度既取决于良好的操作技术，也取决于环境因素。

71
00:04:59,690 --> 00:05:03,250
This video will highlight the most important of these guidelines.
本视频将着重介绍其中最重要的几条准则。

72
00:05:03,250 --> 00:05:07,930
Keep the balance doors closed at all times to prevent air currents from causing the balance
始终关好天平门，防止气流使秤盘

73
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:10,070
pan to bounce slightly.
轻微跳动。

74
00:05:10,070 --> 00:05:15,210
Never lean or lay a hand on the balance table to prevent unstable measurements.
绝不要倚靠天平台或把手放在上面，以免测量不稳定。

75
00:05:15,210 --> 00:05:19,970
Wear gloves to prevent oil from depositing on the glassware, which falsely increases the
戴上手套，防止油脂沉积在玻璃器皿上，使质量

76
00:05:19,970 --> 00:05:21,130
mass.
虚增。

77
00:05:21,130 --> 00:05:24,250
Weigh a chemical directly into the reaction vessel.
把化学品直接称入反应容器中。

78
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:28,370
If that is not possible, use the smallest weigh boat or weigh paper that will hold
如果无法做到，就用能盛放所需量化学品的

79
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:30,570
your desired amount of chemical.
最小的称量舟或称量纸。

80
00:05:30,570 --> 00:05:35,050
Ensure that the outside of the weigh vessel is completely dry before placing it on the
在把称量容器放到秤盘上之前，确保其外部完全干燥，

81
00:05:35,050 --> 00:05:39,690
balance pan and be sure to place the object on the center of the balance pan.
并一定要把物体放在秤盘中央。

82
00:05:39,690 --> 00:05:45,050
Allow moist chemicals to dry completely to avoid elevated readings and avoid breathing
让潮湿的化学品完全干燥，以免读数偏高；也不要对着物体

83
00:05:45,050 --> 00:05:49,770
on an object, which condenses moisture on it and falsely increases its mass.
呼气，那会使水汽在其上凝结，使质量虚增。

84
00:05:49,770 --> 00:05:55,050
Weigh ultra-dry objects or ones immediately removed from a desiccator at identical time
对超干燥的物体或刚从干燥器中取出的物体，要在相同的时间

85
00:05:55,050 --> 00:06:00,210
intervals because they absorb moisture and gain weight the longer they sit in the atmosphere.
间隔进行称量，因为它们在空气中放得越久，吸收的水分越多，重量也越大。

86
00:06:00,210 --> 00:06:05,330
Finally, allow hot or cold objects to reach room temperature before weighing.
最后，要让过热或过冷的物体恢复到室温再称量。

87
00:06:05,330 --> 00:06:10,370
A hot object should be cooled in a desiccator to prevent the pickup of moisture.
热的物体应在干燥器中冷却，以防吸收水分。

88
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:14,530
Hot or cold objects create a convection current in the air around the balance pan,
过热或过冷的物体会在秤盘周围的空气中形成对流，

89
00:06:14,530 --> 00:06:19,330
which reduces the air pressure on the balance pan and results in an unstable reading.
使作用在秤盘上的气压降低，导致读数不稳定。

90
00:06:19,330 --> 00:06:23,690
The accuracy of a measurement is only as good as the instrument that is used.
测量的准确度取决于所用仪器的好坏。

91
00:06:23,690 --> 00:06:28,690
To keep your balance functioning correctly, the following precautions should be taken.
为使天平正常工作，应采取以下预防措施。

92
00:06:28,690 --> 00:06:31,890
Never weigh chemicals directly on the balance pan.
绝不要把化学品直接放在秤盘上称量。

93
00:06:31,890 --> 00:06:36,050
Never add chemicals to the weighing vessel while it is on the balance pan.
称量容器在秤盘上时，绝不要往里面加化学品。

94
00:06:36,050 --> 00:06:40,450
Never pour a chemical directly out of a reagent bottle and into the weigh vessel.
绝不要把化学品直接从试剂瓶倒进称量容器。

95
00:06:40,450 --> 00:06:42,010
Use a spatula instead.
而应使用刮刀。

96
00:06:42,010 --> 00:06:46,650
Pay attention to the maximum weight allowed by a particular balance and do not overload
注意特定天平所允许的最大称量，不要使其

97
00:06:46,650 --> 00:06:47,650
it.
超载。

98
00:06:47,650 --> 00:06:52,490
When using a balance, be aware of the warning signs which indicate that the balance is malfunctioning.
使用天平时，要留意表明天平出现故障的警示迹象。

99
00:06:52,490 --> 00:06:56,570
After recording the weight of a chemical, remove it from the balance pan.
记录完化学品的重量后，把它从秤盘上取下。

100
00:06:56,570 --> 00:07:01,010
The numbers on the display should again read 0.0 milligrams.
显示屏上的数字应重新显示 0.0 毫克。

101
00:07:01,010 --> 00:07:06,610
If the displayed value is 0.3 milligrams or greater, then the zero level was significantly
如果显示值为 0.3 毫克或更大，说明称量过程中零点发生了明显

102
00:07:06,610 --> 00:07:10,210
shifted during the weighing process and the chemical must be re-weighed.
偏移，化学品必须重新称量。

103
00:07:10,210 --> 00:07:12,850
Check the amount of drift that is occurring.
检查漂移的程度。

104
00:07:12,850 --> 00:07:17,450
Drift is characterized by weight readings that do not stabilize or by unstable readings
漂移的特征是重量读数不稳定，或者在不加任何重量时

105
00:07:17,450 --> 00:07:19,410
with no weight applied.
读数也不稳定。

106
00:07:19,410 --> 00:07:23,810
All analytical balances show some degree of fluctuation on their display and care
所有分析天平的显示都会有一定程度的波动，应当

107
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:26,730
should be taken to keep this drift at a minimum.
注意把这种漂移降到最低。

108
00:07:26,730 --> 00:07:31,010
If you notice a change in the amount of instability on a particular balance, then it
如果你注意到某台天平的不稳定程度发生了变化，那就说明它

109
00:07:31,010 --> 00:07:33,050
is malfunctioning.
出了故障。

110
00:07:33,050 --> 00:07:38,210
Drift is affected by two environmental factors, temperature and static electricity.
漂移受两个环境因素影响：温度和静电。

111
00:07:38,210 --> 00:07:41,290
It can be minimized through their manipulation.
通过控制这两个因素，可以将漂移降到最低。

112
00:07:41,290 --> 00:07:44,690
The temperature of the room and the internal temperature of the balance should be kept
室温和天平内部的温度应保持

113
00:07:44,690 --> 00:07:47,890
constant within 2 degrees Celsius.
恒定，波动不超过 2 摄氏度。

114
00:07:47,890 --> 00:07:52,730
Static electricity can be minimized by avoiding the use of plastic containers and by maintaining
要尽量减少静电，可以避免使用塑料容器，并保持

115
00:07:52,730 --> 00:07:55,530
the humidity above 40%.
湿度在 40% 以上。

116
00:07:55,530 --> 00:08:00,450
If you notice excessive drift, the following situations may be occurring.
如果你发现漂移过大，可能是出现了以下情况。

117
00:08:00,450 --> 00:08:03,250
The balance may be exposed to a draft.
天平可能暴露在气流中。

118
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:04,850
Close the doors.
请关好天平门。

119
00:08:04,850 --> 00:08:09,610
The sample may be moist and undergoing evaporation on the balance pan.
样品可能是潮湿的，正在秤盘上蒸发。

120
00:08:09,610 --> 00:08:14,170
The sample might be ultra-dry and absorbing moisture on the balance pan.
样品可能是超干燥的，正在秤盘上吸收水分。

121
00:08:14,170 --> 00:08:19,530
The sample may not be at ambient temperature, which causes it to produce convection currents.
样品可能没有处于环境温度，因而产生对流。

122
00:08:19,530 --> 00:08:22,210
The sample may be electrostatic.
样品可能带有静电。

123
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:26,450
If you notice drift while weighing a sample, the most accurate reading is the first number
如果你在称量样品时发现漂移，最准确的读数是最先出现

124
00:08:26,450 --> 00:08:29,890
that appeared and was maintained for 2 seconds.
并保持了 2 秒的那个数字。

125
00:08:29,890 --> 00:08:33,330
So far, we've discussed the use of a balance for weighing solids.
到目前为止，我们讨论了用天平称量固体。

126
00:08:33,330 --> 00:08:37,370
However, a balance may also be used to weigh liquid samples.
不过，天平也可以用来称量液体样品。

127
00:08:37,370 --> 00:08:42,250
Generally, it is easier and more accurate to determine the volume of a liquid by using
一般来说，用精密的容量玻璃器皿来测定液体的体积，会更容易也更准确，

128
00:08:42,250 --> 00:08:48,890
precision volumetric glassware such as a burette, glass pipette, syringe or automatic pipette
比如滴定管、玻璃移液管、注射器或移液器，

129
00:08:48,890 --> 00:08:52,450
and then use the liquid's density to calculate its mass.
然后再用液体的密度计算其质量。

130
00:08:52,450 --> 00:08:57,530
However, directly measuring the weight of a liquid is preferred in some situations, such
不过，在某些情况下更适合直接测量液体的重量，比如

131
00:08:57,530 --> 00:09:00,050
as when working with a viscous liquid.
处理黏稠液体时。

132
00:09:00,050 --> 00:09:04,730
As a final note, when weighing a volatile liquid or one that evaporates readily, use
最后要注意，称量易挥发或容易蒸发的液体时，要使用

133
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:07,410
a weighing bottle with a lid.
带盖的称量瓶。

134
00:09:07,410 --> 00:09:12,290
Although using a balance is a relatively simple task, accurate measurements can only be ensured
虽然使用天平是一项相对简单的工作，但只有通过良好的操作技术，

135
00:09:12,290 --> 00:09:13,570
through good technique.
才能确保测量准确。

136
00:09:13,570 --> 00:09:17,970
Exceptional care must be taken to maintain a clean environment which helps to keep the
必须格外注意保持环境整洁，这有助于使

137
00:09:17,970 --> 00:09:19,410
balance functioning properly.
天平正常工作。
